---

Step 4 holds the reports of the period. Each report can be exported to Excel.

| Report | What it shows |
|---|---|
| **Management Accounts** | The management accounts for the period. |
| **F5 report** | The one-page GST F5 form from the confirmed figures, with the worksheet and the tax detail as separate attachments. |
| **Trial Balance** | Every account's balance. An account whose balance is on the unexpected side is marked as an abnormal balance. |
| **Control Accounts** | The receivables, payables and other control accounts agreed to their detail. |
| **General Ledger** | Every entry, account by account. |
| **Balance Sheet** / **Profit and Loss** | The financial position and the result for the period. |
| **A/R Aging Detail** / **A/P Aging Detail** | Receivables and payables by age. |

{% screenshot id="bookkeeping/report-trial-balance" caption="The trial balance of ABC PTE. LTD., 30 September 2026." /%}

## F5 report

The F5 report is generated from the figures confirmed under **Review › F5 check**, so it always matches what was confirmed. If the figures have not been confirmed, the page asks for that first.

{% steps %}

1. Confirm the figures under **Review › F5 check**.
2. Generate the F5 report and give it to the client to approve.
3. After the return is filed with IRAS, select **Mark as filed**.

{% /steps %}

To change confirmed figures before filing, select **Withdraw confirmation**, correct the books and confirm again. A filed return cannot be withdrawn: if the books change after filing, the difference is reported in a later return.

{% aside type="note" %}
Operon does not file the F5 with IRAS. Filing is done by the firm, after the client approves the return.
{% /aside %}
